    "id": "train-5914",
    "question": "Salaria is growing oranges this summer. She bought two types of trees. She has 50% of tree A and 50% of tree B. Tree A gives her 10 oranges a month and 60% are good. Tree B gives her 15 oranges and 1/3 are good. If she gets 55 good oranges per month, how many total trees does she have?",
    "gold": "10",
    "answer": "Each tree A gives her six good oranges a month 10 x .6 = <<10*.6=6>>6\nEach tree B gives her five good oranges a month because 15 x (1/3) = <<15*(1/3)=5>>5\nOn average, a tree gives her 5.5 oranges a month because .5(6) + .5(5) = 5.5\nShe has ten total trees because 55 / 5.5 = <<55/5.5=10>>10\n#### 10"
  },
