    "text": "Let x be the number of tree A and y be the number of tree B.\nWe know that x + y = 1 because she has 50% of each type of tree.\nWe also know that 10x * 0.6 + 15y * (1/3) = 55 because 60% of tree A and 1/3 of tree B are good.\nWe can simplify this to 6x + 5y = 55.\nWe can solve this system of equations by substitution or elimination. Let's use substitution.\nWe know that x + y = 1, so x = 1 - y.\nWe can substitute this into the second equation to get 6(1 - y) + 5y = 55.\nExpanding this gives 6 - 6y + 5y = 55.\nCombining like terms gives -y = 49.\nDividing both sides by -1 gives y = -49.\nSubstituting this back into x + y = 1 gives x - 49 = 1.\nAdding 49 to both sides gives x = 50.\nSo Salaria has 50 tree A and 50 tree B.\nThe final answer is \\boxed{100}.",
